{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"a77104dbba9d160f3b8ccc5f03243ab7389dec2b2fc73a4c692cfc952860ee9d","packTokens":5735,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":41,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spec","tokens":5674,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"State, as numbered plain sentences (n = 1, 2, ...), what change this spec asks for. Don't add anything the spec doesn't say. Don't mention IDs.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Feedlot API shall implement every path, HTTP method, parameter, request and response schema, status code, and security rule declared in contracts/openapi.yaml, expose no undocumented API operations, and provide no feedlot product-screen routes or rendered screens.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The API is running and a client has valid contract inputs and any authentication context required by the contract. when The client calls each declared operation using its contract-defined method, path, parameters, and request body. then Each response status and response body field matches the operation's declared contract, including success and error responses.\",\n    \"Given A client calls a protected operation without valid authentication or without contract-required authorization. when The client calls that operation. then The response status is the contract-declared 401 or 403, as applicable, and no undeclared role rule denies an otherwise authorized request.\",\n    \"Given The API host is running. when A client requests an undefined path such as /api/yard or /yard, or uses an unsupported method for a contract path such as POST /api/dashboard. then The response status is 404 for an undefined path or 405 for an unsupported method, and no feedlot product screen is displayed.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an authorized client requests sign-in, session, dashboard, or lot-list operations, the Feedlot API shall return the contract-defined authentication, current-user, dashboard, and filtered lot values.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A client has valid sign-in credentials and no bearer token. when The client sends POST /api/auth/sign-in with the contract SignInRequest body. then The response status is 200 and the response contains the contract-defined accessToken and user fields, including declared permissions and authorizedYards.\",\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token. when The client sends GET /api/session. then The response status is 200 and the response user field contains the current user and contract-defined permissions.\",\n    \"Given Authorized dashboard data and a valid rankBy value of fcr, adg, or costOfGain are available. when The client sends GET /api/dashboard with the selected rankBy value. then The response status is 200 and the response rankingMeasure, bestLots, and worstLots correspond to the selected measure.\",\n    \"Given Lots have distinct pen, breed, sex, and status values and the client has a valid bearer token. when The client sends GET /api/lots with supported query filters. then The response status is 200 and the response lots list contains only rows matching the supplied filters and contract-defined fields.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an authorized client previews or imports procurement records or saves allocations, the Feedlot API shall return and persist contract-defined PO-line-to-lot and lot-to-pen traceability, including import matching and allocation-conflict results.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token and the source adapter is available. when The client sends GET /api/imports/source-records. then The response status is 200 and the response records field is a list of available procurement and receiving records.\",\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token and submits a valid ImportRequest selecting source records. when The client sends POST /api/imports. then The response status is 200 and the response contains status, createdCount, updatedCount, records, and allocationConflicts fields reflecting the selected records and current matches.\",\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token and valid PO-line-to-lot and lot-to-pen allocation quantities. when The client calls PUT /api/allocations and then GET /api/allocations. then Both response statuses are 200 and the response poLines, lotPens, and pens contain the saved quantities, traceability status, and capacity information.\",\n    \"Given A client submits an invalid selection, conflicting import, or allocation that violates saved state. when The client submits the relevant import or allocation request. then The response status and error response match the operation's declared 409 or 422 contract.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an authorized client requests lot forecasts, forecast-setting updates, metrics, insights, planner actions, or weight-history operations, the Feedlot API shall return contract-defined values, calculations, explainable suggestions, and persisted updates.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token and the requested lot exists. when The client sends GET /api/lots/{lotId}/forecast. then The response status is 200 and the response contains the lot forecast values, forecastBasis, and effective yard and lot assumptions.\",\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token and submits a valid ForecastSettingsRequest. when The client sends PATCH /api/forecast-settings or PATCH /api/lots/{lotId}/forecast-settings for an existing lot. then The response status is 200 and the response contains persisted setting values; a subsequent forecast response contains the effective assumptions and projectedMarketDate declared by the contract.\",\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token and the requested lot exists with feeding and weight records where applicable. when The client sends GET /api/lots/{lotId}/metrics or GET /api/lots/{lotId}/insights. then The response status is 200 and the response contains contract-defined metrics or suggestions with their basis, including null unavailable metric values where applicable.\",\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token, an existing lot, and a valid planner-selected insight action or WeightMeasurementRequest. when The client sends POST /api/lots/{lotId}/insights/actions, GET /api/lots/{lotId}/weights, or POST /api/lots/{lotId}/weights as applicable. then The response status and response fields match the contract, and the returned action or measurement is present in the subsequent relevant response.\",\n    \"Given A client submits a weight measurement that fails contract validation, or requests forecast data or settings for a nonexistent lot. when The client sends the applicable weight, forecast, or forecast-settings request. then The response status is the contract-declared 422 with VALIDATION_ERROR for invalid measurement data or 404 with NOT_FOUND for a nonexistent lot.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an authorized client reads or changes inventory, the Feedlot API shall return contract-defined stock, movement, projection, and export values and persist valid inventory changes in PostgreSQL.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token and inventory items or movements exist, or the inventory is empty. when The client sends GET /api/inventory. then The response status is 200 and the response contains operationalTotals, items, movements, and contract-defined stock fields.\",\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token and submits a valid InventoryItemRequest for creation or update. when The client sends POST /api/inventory/items or PATCH /api/inventory/items/{itemId}. then The response status is 201 for creation or 200 for update and the response item contains the saved contract fields and stock values.\",\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token and submits a valid receipt or adjustment InventoryMovementRequest for an existing item. when The client sends POST /api/inventory/movements. then The response status is 201 and the response contains the saved movement and item with updated stock values.\",\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token, a supported horizon, and inventory with applicable plans and wastage settings. when The client sends GET /api/inventory/projections separately for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, semiAnnual, and annual horizons. then Each response status is 200 and each response contains the selected horizon, projection rows with projected consumption and balance, and movement distinctions.\",\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token and submits an inventory request that fails contract validation or a projection horizon outside the contract enum. when The client sends the applicable inventory write or projection request. then The response status is 422 and the response error code is VALIDATION_ERROR.\",\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token and authorized operational inventory rows exist. when The client sends GET /api/inventory/export. then The response status is 200 and the response contains fileName, contentType text/csv, and a Base64 CSV file derived from operational records.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an authorized client reads, creates, revises, optimizes, or approves a ration, the Feedlot API shall return contract-defined ration data and optimization or approval results and persist valid ration changes.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token and saved ration definitions exist, or the ration collection is empty. when The client sends GET /api/rations. then The response status is 200 and the response rations list contains saved ingredient, proportion, nutrition, cost, and approval fields.\",\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token and submits a valid RationRequest for creation or revision. when The client sends POST /api/rations or PATCH /api/rations/{rationId}. then The response status is 201 for creation or 200 for revision and the response ration contains the persisted definition and calculated contract fields, including costPerPound where declared.\",\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token and submits a valid ration optimization request with candidate mixes and nutrition requirements. when The client sends POST /api/rations/optimization. then The response status is 200 and the response contains the contract optimization result and cost comparison, including the lowest-cost qualifying candidate or qualifyingMixFound=false as applicable.\",\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token and the requested ration exists in a state eligible for approval. when The client sends POST /api/rations/{rationId}/approval. then The response status is 200 and the response contains the rationId and updated approvalStatus, which is Approved where specified by the contract.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an authorized client reads, creates, reviews, or changes the execution status of a feed plan, the Feedlot API shall return and persist contract-defined pen-level plan details, calculated quantities, audit state, and status.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token and saved feed plans exist, or the plan collection is empty. when The client sends GET /api/feed-plans. then The response status is 200 and the response plans list contains saved plan details, execution state, and audit-related fields.\",\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token and submits a valid FeedPlanRequest with dated pen, ration, bunk rate, and animal-count values. when The client sends POST /api/feed-plans. then The response status is 201 and the response plan contains calculated planned quantity, quantity per animal, total feed cost, expected energy intake, and status fields.\",\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token, an existing plan, and a valid PlanReviewRequest or PlanStatusRequest. when The client sends POST /api/feed-plans/{planId}/review or PATCH /api/feed-plans/{planId}/status. then The response status is 200 and the response plan contains the saved reviewRequired value or requested execution status.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an authorized client records, corrects, or voids a feeding event, the Feedlot API shall persist the event and return its contract-defined variance, cost, energy, inventory movements, and updated lot feed totals.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token and saved feeding events and lot allocations exist, or the event collection is empty. when The client sends GET /api/feeding-events. then The response status is 200 and the response events list contains saved activity, lot allocations, and inventory movements.\",\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token and submits a valid FeedingEventRequest with planned and delivered quantities. when The client sends POST /api/feeding-events. then The response status is 201 and the response contains the saved event, variance equal to deliveredQuantity minus plannedQuantity, calculated cost and energy, inventoryMovements, and updated lotFeedTotals.\",\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token, an existing feeding event, and a valid correction request or an event eligible to be voided. when The client sends PATCH /api/feeding-events/{eventId} or POST /api/feeding-events/{eventId}/void. then The response status is 200 and the response event has the applicable Corrected or Voided status with corresponding reversal or correction movements and recalculated lotFeedTotals.\",\n    \"Given A client submits a feeding event that conflicts with current inventory or fails contract validation. when The client sends POST /api/feeding-events. then The response status is the contract-declared 409 or 422 and the response contains the contract ApiError fields.\",\n    \"Given A feeding event has been successfully saved and the App PostgreSQL database is available. when The API process restarts and the client reads the event and inventory. then The response contains the saved event and corresponding stock and lot totals.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an authorized client requests an operational, feed-to-gain, or profitability report or export, the Feedlot API shall return contract-defined permission-filtered rows, calculations, summaries, and requested export artifacts.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token and operational feeding, performance, and inventory data with supported filters. when The client sends GET /api/reports/operational or GET /api/reports/operational/export. then The response status is 200 and the response rows and summary match the filters, or the response contains a CSV file derived only from the authorized filtered rows.\",\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token and supplies a required date range plus optional breed, sex, or pen filters. when The client sends GET /api/reports/feed-to-gain. then The response status is 200 and the response rows contain contract-defined ADG, feed, FCR, cost-of-gain, and energy fields for matching lots.\",\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token and supplies a valid feed-to-gain date range, supported filters, and format csv or pdf. when The client sends GET /api/reports/feed-to-gain/export. then The response status is 200 and the response file artifact has contentType and content corresponding to the requested format and filtered authorized rows.\",\n    \"Given A client omits a required feed-to-gain date or supplies an export format outside the contract enum. when The client sends a feed-to-gain report or export request. then The response status is 422 and the response error code is VALIDATION_ERROR.\",\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token and supplies supported profitability horizon, breed, penId, or roiStatus filters. when The client sends GET /api/reports/profitability or GET /api/reports/profitability/export. then The response status is 200 and the response contains authorized matching profitability rows and canViewProfitability where declared, or a CSV file with those filtered authorized rows.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an authorized client reads, loads, resets, or replaces sample records, the Feedlot API shall return contract-defined sample status and records, avoid duplicate loading, and require explicit confirmation for reset or replacement.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token and sample records may be absent, not yet loaded, or already loaded. when The client sends GET /api/sample-data or POST /api/sample-data/load. then The response status is 200 and the response loaded, recordCount, records, and load status distinguish an empty set, a successful load, and already_loaded without duplicating records.\",\n    \"Given A client has a valid bearer token and sends reset or replacement first without required confirmation and then with explicit confirmation. when The client sends POST /api/sample-data/reset or POST /api/sample-data/replace. then The unconfirmed response status is the contract-declared 422 or 409, and the confirmed response has the completed operation status and resulting recordCount.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Feedlot API shall store contract domain data in PostgreSQL using the configured connection string named App and preserve successful writes across API process restarts.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The API is configured with an App PostgreSQL connection and a client successfully creates or updates a contract resource. when The API process restarts and the client retrieves the resource through its contract-defined read operation. then The response contains the saved value and the returned record has the same id and field values as the successful write response.\",\n    \"Given The API is configured with a connection string named App and a successful contract write has completed. when A test queries the configured PostgreSQL database for the affected entity. then A row with the values written by the request is present in the App database.\",\n    \"Given The API starts with a configured App PostgreSQL connection. when Startup creates the database schema. then A row exists in PostgreSQL for each persisted record type required by the implemented contract operations.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When Seed:Demo is true, the Feedlot API shall use SeedData.Run at startup to insert 3 to 5 believable, contract-example-derived sample rows per application table when that table is empty, leave nonempty tables unchanged, and fail startup while surfacing any seed-write error.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A fresh, empty App PostgreSQL database has Seed:Demo true. when The API starts successfully. then A database query reads 3 to 5 believable sample rows derived from corresponding contract examples in each application table, and each corresponding API collection response contains a nonempty list.\",\n    \"Given A contract-backed application table already contains operational rows and Seed:Demo is true. when The API starts and runs SeedData.Run. then The pre-existing row values are unchanged and no seed rows are added to that nonempty table.\",\n    \"Given Seed:Demo is true and PostgreSQL rejects a seed write during startup. when The API starts. then Startup fails and the surfaced error identifies the seed-write failure without reporting successful readiness.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When Seed:Demo is false and persisted collections are empty, the Feedlot API shall serve contract collection operations without requiring or assuming demo-seed rows, and the API test suite shall create its own records when non-empty data is required.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An isolated App PostgreSQL database has no records and Seed:Demo is false. when An authorized client calls contract collection endpoints, including GET /api/lots, GET /api/inventory, GET /api/rations, GET /api/feed-plans, and GET /api/feeding-events. then Each response status is 200 and each response collection field is an empty list rather than an error or an assumed demo record.\",\n    \"Given Seed:Demo is false and a test creates its own records through contract write operations. when The test reads the corresponding contract list operation. then The response list contains the test-created records without depending on demo-seed record ids, counts, or values.\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  \"Successful API writes to contract domain data use PostgreSQL durability and remain available after an API process restart.\"\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\nRestate the change."}